---
title: Let Things Be
description: Let things be even it doesn't always work.
publishedAt: 2026-11-22
draft: false
tags: []
---
I often assume that putting enough effort into something will yield an equal result, but that isn't always the case. You can keep trying in different ways, test new approaches, and still end up disappointed by the outcome. Sometimes things fall apart in ways you never could have predicted. Even our best calculations fall short and the urge to control every variable is usually just fear in disguise.

Some outcomes are completely immune to how much you care or how hard you try. People have their own agendas, goals, and destinations. If you aren't what they're looking for, no amount of genuine care will change that. Showing up more won't suddenly make them change their mind. The more I tried to force affection, the more it chipped away at my self-respect. They might still be nice because they don't want to hurt you, and it might not even be anyone's fault. Sometimes it's just the way things are and the wisest move is to step back and give the disappointment room to fade.

This doesn't only apply to relationships; it shows up in any goal you chase. Most of life operates on probabilistic systems, not linear ones. Accepting that helps me see things more clearly. I don't have to lower my standards or give up on trying. The timeline sits on its own, so it's better to do my part, let go of when it might pay off, and stay ready to adapt to whatever actually happens.
